Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:18:17 +0300
Subject: reverb: Dattorro's output taps without a division per tap

The Dattorro plate reverb (the default engine, "dat") reads 14 output taps every sample, and
each tap's position was wrapped with an integer division (index %= size). The PS3's PPE
divides in tens of cycles without pipelining, so the wrap cost more than the reverb's
arithmetic. line_out is always in [0, size) and every tap is shorter than its line, so one
conditional subtraction gives the same index; the division stays for any other case. The
output is bit-identical.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/rvoice/fluid_rev_dattorro.cpp b/src/rvoice/fluid_rev_dattorro.cpp
--- a/src/rvoice/fluid_rev_dattorro.cpp
+++ b/src/rvoice/fluid_rev_dattorro.cpp
@@ -91,10 +91,20 @@ static float fluid_dattorro_read_tap(const fluid_reverb_delay_line<float> &delay
     }
 
     int index = delay.line_out + tap;
-    index %= size;
-    if(index < 0)
+    /* PS3: line_out is in [0, size) and every tap is shorter than its line, so one subtraction
+     * wraps it; the division stays for anything else. The PPE's integer divide takes tens of
+     * cycles and this ran 14 times a sample. */
+    if(index >= size && index - size < size && tap >= 0)
     {
-        index += size;
+        index -= size;
+    }
+    else if(index >= size || index < 0)
+    {
+        index %= size;
+        if(index < 0)
+        {
+            index += size;
+        }
     }
     return delay.line[index];
 }
